  novelty_killer:        green (A) — C has FATAL_COLLISION (mechanism error + PROJ-0002/DEAD-0016 overlap); A survives prior-art separation
  product_realist:       green (A) — 63.3%/86.1% tool-result mass is actionable for serving operators; C narrower scope
  systems_reviewer:      yellow (A) — A is insight contribution; C weak because shipping caches key on token prefix not path
  theory_skeptic:        yellow (A) — A wins on killability + positive-producibility; overclaims "serving dollar" from token-mass

PRIOR_ART_ADEQUATE: yes-with-caveat
  Novelty killer disclosed web-search was denied; cited prior art from known retrievable arXiv records
  (DistServe 2401.09670, SplitWise 2311.18677, Parrot 2405.19888, Autellix 2502.13965, RadixAttention
  2312.07104, vLLM-APC 2309.06180, PromptCache 2311.04934, Sarathi-Serve 2403.02310). Coverage spans
  disaggregation, prefix caching, and agent serving — the relevant landscape. Separation argument is
  clean: NONE of these measure the prefill/decode token-mass split on real agent traces. Adequate for
  GREEN, but L0 pre-registration MUST cite and one-line differentiate each (per novelty_killer fix #2).

FATAL_OBJECTIONS: []
  No reviewer RED on Charter A. Both YELLOWs (systems_reviewer, theory_skeptic) are methodological
  precision issues resolvable at pre-registration time, not viability threats.

CHARTER_C_KILL_RATIONALE:
  Three independent fatal findings, each sufficient alone, all unrebutted:
  1. MECHANISM MISCHARACTERIZATION (novelty_killer, evaluation_prosecutor, systems_reviewer): RadixAttention
     (2312.07104) and vLLM-APC (2309.06180) are CONTENT-ADDRESSED — they key on token IDs / block hashes.
     Changed file content produces different tokens, yielding a cache MISS, not a "stale hit serving wrong
     KV." C's thesis sentence ("a hit would serve wrong KV / must be invalidated") describes a failure mode
     that CANNOT OCCUR in production systems. This is not a framing quibble — it is the load-bearing premise.
  2. DEGENERATE MEASUREMENT (theory_skeptic): Codex changed-content LB95 = 1.000 with undisclosed N for
     repeated same-path reads. If N is small, RE-C0 fails and the claim has no denominator. The headline
     is dominated by the trivial read-after-WRITE case: "agents edit files they read, ergo files change"
     restates the input, not a serving finding.
  3. COLLISION + MINED-OUT ESCAPE (novelty_killer, theory_skeptic): With the strawman premise removed, C
     reduces to "APC miss-rate on file-read prefixes" — which COLLIDES with PROJ-0002 (reuse under edits)
     and is adjacent to DEAD-0016 (byte-identical repeats). RE-C4's predictor (write-between-reads predicts
     staleness) drags C into the DEAD-0017..0021 mined-out predictability axis.

REQUIRED_EVIDENCE: []
  All pre-measured numbers cited in Charter A's packet (63.3% CC / 86.1% Codex result mass; per-session
  median 0.699/0.848; top-decile 78.8%/57.2%; Gini 0.864/0.746; LB95 0.502/0.845) were pre-measured on
  live corpora. No additional evidence needed before seeding; L0 experiment will produce the definitive
  numbers under the tightened gates below.

MANDATORY_BASELINES:
  - Standard chat traces (e.g., ShareGPT or equivalent multi-turn conversational dataset) — must show
    the prefill/decode mass split is structurally different for agent tool-loops vs chat (evaluation_prosecutor)
  - DistServe 2401.09670 assumed workload mix — cite the assumed prefill/decode ratio and show the measured
    agent ratio diverges (novelty_killer, product_realist)

MANDATORY_FIXES (binding — L0 pre-registration MUST honor all):
  1. REFRAME THESIS (theory_skeptic, unanimous support): STRIKE "where the agent serving dollar is spent."
     Replace with "where the agent serving prefill TOKEN MASS is spent." Token mass ≠ cost mass (prefill
     is ~10-100x cheaper per token than decode per DistServe/Splitwise). Add OPTIONAL secondary RE-A4:
     cost-weighted variant using a published prefill-vs-decode $/token ratio (cite Splitwise 2311.18677
     or DistServe 2401.09670), reported as SECONDARY, not headline.
  2. CONTRIBUTION FRAMING (novelty_killer): Pre-register the contribution as the GRANULAR decomposition
     (tool-result vs arg vs decode-interstitial) + heavy-tail Gini + cross-instrument replication.
     Explicitly concede "prefill-heavy" is already assumed by DistServe/SplitWise — the bare direction
     is NOT the claim. Reject any reading of A as "rediscovers prefill-heaviness."
  3. RE-A2 DENOMINATOR COMMITMENT (theory_skeptic, evaluation_prosecutor): The MOST-CONSERVATIVE
     denominator (assistant-text-block-only) is the HEADLINE. The other two denominators (raw span,
     non-result mass) are robustness checks. If the conservative denominator drops below 50%, downgrade
     to "largest single component," not "majority." Commit BEFORE seeing the conservative number.
  4. STATIC vs DYNAMIC SEPARATION (evaluation_prosecutor): Distinguish static system-prompt prefix
     (consumes KV memory after turn 1 but zero marginal compute) from dynamic per-turn tool-result
     prefill (consumes both). Report both shares; the "tool-result dominated" claim refers to the
     DYNAMIC marginal prefill, not total KV memory.
  5. CROSS-INSTRUMENT EQUIVALENCE MARGIN (theory_skeptic): RE-A3 must specify an a-priori margin.
     Proposed: both LB95 > 0.50 AND |CC − Codex| < 0.40 on the chosen denominator. If only the
     direction replicates but magnitudes diverge beyond margin, report as "instrument-dependent
     magnitude," not "replicated dominance."
  6. GINI WITH CIs (theory_skeptic): Report Gini with bootstrap CI (2000x session-clustered) and a
     bootstrap CI on the CC-Codex Gini delta. Do not headline point estimates without CIs.
  7. OPERATIONAL DEFINITIONS (theory_skeptic): Pin "tool-result" / "arg" / "decode-interstitial" to
     parse_cc_session / parse_codex_session field names IN the L0 pre-registration. Disclose the
     tokenizer (or explicit char-proxy) and pre-register it.
  8. CLEAN-NEGATIVE CRITERION EXPANSION (theory_skeptic): Clean negative is NOT just "LB95 < 0.50."
     Also: "Gini < 0.5 on either corpus" (= no heavy tail = boring uniform distribution, no cacheable
     hot spots).
  9. MANDATORY RELATED WORK (novelty_killer): Cite and one-line differentiate DistServe, SplitWise,
     DuetServe, Sarathi-Serve, Parrot, Autellix, RadixAttention, vLLM-APC. Each: "does not measure
     the prefill/decode token-mass split of real agent tool-loops."

MAP_DELTA_PROPOSAL:
